sw-global-war-supply-failure-funds = Not enough available war funds. There is no automatic refill or debt.
sw-global-war-supply-failure-quota = Not enough allowance remains in this window's decision.
sw-global-war-supply-failure-revision = Data or the production recipe changed. Check the current state.
sw-global-war-supply-failure-localonly = There is no new market allocation. Local stock requires separate authority.
sw-global-war-supply-failure-rate = The current program has paused output on this line.
sw-global-war-supply-failure-transfer = Physical transfer was not completed. Check containers and free space.
sw-global-war-supply-failure-existingsupply = Existing stock or unfinished production already covers the total production target. Local stock is not automatically requisitioned.
sw-global-war-supply-failure-denied = Your current assignment does not permit this operation.
